[particle_id]\n        if p.status\"'!='\"'active':\n            raise InvalidActionError('inactive')\n        cur=self._step(p.time); tgt=self._step(target_time)\n        if tgt<=cur: raise InvalidActionError('non advancing')\n        cost=tgt-cur\n        if self._spent + cost > self.budget: raise BudgetExceededError()\n        self._spent += cost\n        p.time=self.time_grid[tgt]\n        if tgt==len(self.time_grid)-1:\n            p.status='completed'\n        return p\n    def preview(self, particle_id, mode='clean_anchor', scorer='default'):\n        p=self._particles[particle_id]\n        if p.status=='pruned': raise InvalidActionError('pruned')\n        if self._spent + 1 > self.budget: raise BudgetExceededError()\n        self._spent += 1\n        aid=self._next_aid; self._next_aid+=1\n        base_scores={0:0.52,1:0.49,2:0.51,3:0.55,4:0.50,5:0.48,6:0.53,7:0.47}\n        base=base_scores.get(particle_id, 0.50)\n        score=base + 0.02*p.time - 0.01*((particle_id+aid)%2)\n        uncertainty=max(0.0, 1.0-p.time)\n        pr=Preview(id=aid, particle_id=particle_id, time=p.time, score=score, uncertainty=uncertainty)\n        self._previews[aid]=pr\n        p.last_preview_id=aid\n        return pr\n    def backward(self, anchor_id, target_time, noise_policy='fresh_noise', num_children=1, mask=None, strength=1.0):\n        if num_children<=0: raise InvalidActionError('bad children')\n        anchor=self._previews[anchor_id]\n        out=[]\n        for _ in range(num_children):\n            pid=self._next_pid; self._next_pid+=1\n            self._particles[pid]=Particle(id=pid, time=target_time, status='active')\n            out.append(pid)\n        return out\n    def prune(self, particle_ids):\n        for pid in particle_ids:\n            p=self._particles[pid]\n            if p.status=='completed': raise InvalidActionError('completed')\n            p.status='pruned'\n    def answer(self, rule='best_preview_score'):\n        class Ans:\n            def __init__(self, nfe, rule):\n                self.nfe_used=nfe; self.rule=rule; self.event_log=[]\n        return Ans(self._spent, rule)\n\nfor beta in [0.0,0.25,0.5,0.75,1.0]:\n    env=FakeEnv()\n    ans=OptimalController().solve(env,beta)\n    print(beta, ans.nfe_used)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"0.0 10\n0.25 20\n0.5 36\n0.75 48\n1.0 64\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented a new ambiguity-aware controller in [optimal.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py). The idea is a champion/challenger policy: start with cheap multi-root scouts, rank by preview, then use late budget differently depending on evidence. If the top preview is ambiguous against the runner-up, spend on challenger continuation and preserving width; if the leader is clear, spend on local backward refinement around the leader. This is meant to repair the current weakness at mid/high beta where recent controllers were mostly single-root sequential confirmation and still lost to the beta-matched ODE baseline at `0.5/0.75/1.0`.\n\nI inspected the required sources: the implementation spec, the injected context pack, current [optimal.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py), [baselines.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/baselines.py), [state.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/core/state.py), [errors.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/core/errors.py), and the compact prior snapshots/summaries for `r0000` and `r0001`. The latest frontier rows I used were:\n- `beta=0.00`: reward `0.728363`, mean NFE `10.0`, above baseline\n- `beta=0.25`: reward `0.822718`, mean NFE `19.944`, above baseline\n- `beta=0.50`: reward `0.834361`, mean NFE `34.760`, below baseline `0.836650`\n- `beta=0.75`: reward `0.837577`, mean NFE `45.000`, below baseline `0.843990`\n- `beta=1.00`: reward `0.840356`, mean NFE `61.364`, below baseline `0.847290`\n\nThe last two snapshots did make a real change, but mostly within the same family: both were preview-heavy single-root or near-single-root confirm/refine policies with only modestly different thresholds and child usage. The new behavioral mechanism is different in two ways:\n- explicit ambiguity-driven allocation between challenger continuation and leader refinement;\n- beta-shaped multi-root width retained longer at mid/high beta instead of collapsing early and then spending mostly on repeated late previews.\n\nExact beta schedule:\n- `beta=0.00`: target `10`, single-root probe, `5` step+preview pairs. Locked low-beta behavior.\n- `beta=0.25`: target `20`, roots `3`, scout keep `2`, mid count `2`, ambiguity tail chooses either both contenders to step `0.6` or champion to `0.7` plus runner-up to `0.5`.\n- `beta=0.50`: target `36`, roots `4`, scout keep `3`, mid count `3`, late count `2`, no mandatory final pair, clear-winner case allows `1` refinement child.\n- `beta=0.75`: target `48`, roots `4`, scout keep `3`, mid count `3`, late count `2`, final count `2`, mixed-noise refinement, up to `2` ambiguous or `3` confident children.\n- `beta=1.00`: target `64`, roots `4`, scout keep `4`, mid count `4`, late count `3`, final count `2`, mixed-noise refinement, up to `3` ambiguous or `4` confident children.\n\nBudget use is monotonic because every behavior-critical knob is nondecreasing with beta: target NFE, retained width, number of late confirmations, and refinement allowance. Low beta uses no backward children; mid beta introduces bounded leader repair; high beta preserves more contenders and spends more on refinement only after preview evidence.\n\nTarget-NFE reflection:\n- `beta=0.00`, ceiling/band `[10,10]`: underuse is not acceptable here, so the schedule is fixed to exactly 10 via five step+preview probes. Expected to stay on target.\n- `beta=0.25`, ceiling/band `[18,20]`: earlier proposals already beat baseline, but underuse would be unjustified if it came from stopping after early scouts. I adjusted the tail so ambiguity spends on two contenders and clarity spends on champion plus runner-up. Expected to land near 20 without pointless actions.\n- `beta=0.50`, ceiling/band `[32,36]`: this was a weak region and prior underuse looked like conservative allocation, not justified stopping. I added a structured late stage plus one clear-winner refinement path so the controller can use the full mid-budget regime productively. Expected near 36.\n- `beta=0.75`, ceiling/band `[44,48]`: prior controller was in-band but still weak versus ODE. Underuse here is mostly unjustified because more selective challenger confirmation or repair could help. The new policy keeps width longer and only refines after evidence. Expected near 48.\n- `beta=1.00`, ceiling/band `[60,64]`: prior controller was in-band but still weak. Extra compute should go to evidence-ranked width and bounded leader repair, not more blind late previews. The new tail does that and should spend near 64 without overshoot.\n\nExpected improvement target:\n- primary: `beta=0.75` and `beta=1.0`, where the current policy is still clearly below the beta-matched ODE reward despite comparable NFE;\n- secondary: `beta=0.5`, where the deficit is smaller but still negative and looks repairable by better allocation rather than more raw spend.\n\nChecks run:\n- `python -m py_compile flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py`\n- dry run on the public core env\n- dry run on a tiny fake env with SD3.5-like step-cost semantics to verify target-NFE discipline; realized NFE was `10/20/36/48/64` for betas `0/0.25/0.5/0.75/1.0`\n\nMain risks:\n- ambiguity thresholds may preserve challengers too long at `0.75/1.0`, reducing depth on the eventual best branch;\n- mixed-noise repair could still hurt if PickScore is more sensitive to anchor fidelity than local diversity;\n- low-beta `0.25` is already above baseline, so the extra confirmation logic could slightly trade away reward-per-NFE if previews are noisier than expected."}}
