{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py | sed -n '261,420p'\"","aggregated_output":"   261\t            preview = self._latest_preview_from_state(state, particle_id)\n   262\t            if preview is None or preview.score is None:\n   263\t                particle = state.particles.get(particle_id)\n   264\t                time_value = float(particle.time) if particle is not None else 0.0\n   265\t                return (float(\"-inf\"), float(\"-inf\"), time_value, -particle_id)\n   266\t            return (\n   267\t                float(preview.score),\n   268\t                -float(preview.uncertainty or 0.0),\n   269\t                float(preview.time),\n   270\t                -particle_id,\n   271\t            )\n   272\t\n   273\t        return sorted(particle_ids, key=key, reverse=True)\n   274\t\n   275\t    def _rank_latest_previews(self, env: FlowTTSEnv) -> list[PreviewRecord]:\n   276\t        state = env.get_state()\n   277\t        latest: list[PreviewRecord] = []\n   278\t        for particle in state.particles.values():\n   279\t            if particle.last_preview_id is None:\n   280\t                continue\n   281\t            preview = state.previews.get(particle.last_preview_id)\n   282\t            if preview is None or preview.score is None:\n   283\t                continue\n   284\t            latest.append(preview)\n   285\t        return sorted(\n   286\t            latest,\n   287\t            key=lambda preview: (\n   288\t                float(preview.score),\n   289\t                -float(preview.uncertainty or 0.0),\n   290\t                float(preview.time),\n   291\t                -preview.particle_id,\n   292\t            ),\n   293\t            reverse=True,\n   294\t        )\n   295\t\n   296\t    def _latest_preview(self, env: FlowTTSEnv, particle_id: int) -> PreviewRecord | None:\n   297\t        return self._latest_preview_from_state(env.get_state(), particle_id)\n   298\t\n   299\t    def _latest_preview_from_state(\n   300\t        self,\n   301\t        state,\n   302\t        particle_id: int,\n   303\t    ) -> PreviewRecord | None:\n   304\t        particle = state.particles.get(particle_id)\n   305\t        if particle is None or particle.last_preview_id is None:\n   306\t            return None\n   307\t        return state.previews.get(particle.last_preview_id)\n   308\t\n   309\t    def _child_finish_preview_cost(self, env: FlowTTSEnv, step_index: int) -> int:\n   310\t        target_step = max(0, min(step_index, len(env.time_grid) - 1))\n   311\t        return max(0, (len(env.time_grid) - 1) - target_step) + 1\n   312\t\n   313\t    def _require_budget(self, env: FlowTTSEnv, target_nfe: int, needed: int) -> None:\n   314\t        if needed <= 0:\n   315\t            return\n   316\t        if env.budget_left < needed or self._spent(env) + needed > target_nfe:\n   317\t            raise BudgetExceededError(\"target compute band reached\")\n   318\t\n   319\t    def _step_index(self, env: FlowTTSEnv, time_value: float) -> int:\n   320\t        return min(\n   321\t            range(len(env.time_grid)),\n   322\t            key=lambda index: abs(float(env.time_grid[index]) - float(time_value)),\n   323\t        )\n   324\t\n   325\t    def _time_at_step(self, env: FlowTTSEnv, step_index: int) -> float:\n   326\t        bounded = max(0, min(step_index, len(env.time_grid) - 1))\n   327\t        return float(env.time_grid[bounded])\n   328\t\n   329\t    def _spent(self, env: FlowTTSEnv) -> int:\n   330\t        return max(0, int(env.budget - env.budget_left))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented a new controller in [flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py#L10). The idea is a beta-shaped late-duel policy: low beta stays cheap and mostly deterministic, mid/high beta explicitly keeps multiple roots alive deeper, and only `beta=1.0` gets one ambiguity-triggered late backward repair from a late preview anchor instead of repeated broad refinement. The key behavioral change is in the staged multi-root schedule at [optimal.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py#L48) plus the late repair gate at [optimal.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py#L128).\n\nI inspected the injected baseline/frontier rows in the context pack, especially latest `r0002` results: `beta=0.0` reward `0.785184` at `10` NFE, `0.25` reward `0.812771` at `20`, `0.5` reward `0.835907` at `36`, `0.75` reward `0.837277` at `46.752`, `1.0` reward `0.840382` at `61.884`; and compared them to the injected ODE baselines `0.676462/0.802083/0.836650/0.843990/0.847290` at `10/20/36/48/64`. Weakest relative regimes were `beta=0.75` and `beta=1.0`, with `0.5` slightly below baseline and `0/0.25` already above. I also checked the `r0001` and `r0002` controller snapshots; they were real behavioral changes, but the resulting frontier still mostly collapsed to single-root preview behavior for low and mid beta, and the extra high-beta backward allocation did not close the baseline gap.\n\nExact beta schedule:\n- `beta=0.0`: single track, target `10`, probe steps `1..5` for `5 forward + 5 preview = 10`.\n- `beta=0.25`: `2` roots, stages `(step,count,keep) = (1,2,2) -> (4,2,1) -> (7,1,1) -> (10,1,1)`, target `20`.\n- `beta=0.5`: `4` roots, stages `(1,4,3) -> (4,3,2) -> (8,2,2) -> (10,2,2)`, target `36`.\n- `beta=0.75`: `4` roots, stages `(1,4,4) -> (5,4,3) -> (8,3,2) -> (9,2,2) -> (10,2,2)`, target `48`.\n- `beta=1.0`: `4` roots, stages `(1,4,4) -> (4,4,4) -> (7,4,4) -> (9,4,4) -> (10,4,4)`, target `64`, plus at most one late repair child from step `8` if late previews are close or still uncertain.\n\nBudget use is monotonic because beta only increases target NFE, root width, survivor depth, and optional repair; no higher beta removes a lower-beta compute path. The novelty relative to recent best is that compute is shifted from single-track repeated previewing and multiple late refinements into an explicit late-duel mechanism: preserve challenger diversity deeper at `0.75/1.0`, prune by score-gap only after evidence, and allow only one ambiguity-conditioned backward repair instead of broad child spawning.\n\nChecks run:\n- `python -m py_compile flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py`\n- a tiny fake-env dry run exercising the public API; realized NFE was `10, 20, 36, 48, 63` for betas `0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0`.\n\nExpected risks: PickScore early previews may still mis-rank roots, so the stronger multi-root path could underperform if early noise dominates; and the single repair child at `1.0` may be too conservative if broader local search is actually needed. This round is mainly aimed at improving `beta=0.75` first, then `beta=1.0`, while keeping `0.25` safe and avoiding the small `0.5` underperformance.\n\nPer-beta underuse reflection and target-band fit:\n- `beta=0.0`, ceiling/band `10 / [10,10]`: no underuse; schedule is exactly `10`.\n- `beta=0.25`, ceiling/band `20 / [18,20]`: no underuse; schedule is exactly `20`. I kept it tight because prior history showed extra forward/prune churn here hurt reward.\n- `beta=0.5`, ceiling/band `36 / [32,36]`: prior latest was on target already; schedule is exactly `36`. Extra utilization was not the problem, allocation was.\n- `beta=0.75`, ceiling/band `48 / [44,48]`: prior latest used `46.752` and still lagged baseline. I adjusted utilization upward to a structured `48` by keeping two contenders alive to steps `9` and `10`, rather than adding more backward children.\n- `beta=1.0`, ceiling/band `64 / [60,64]`: prior latest used `61.884`; the new core path uses `60`, and the late repair lifts it to `63` when evidence says it is useful. That small slack is intentional to stay below the hard ceiling without meaningless filler actions."}}
