{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented a new staged controller in [optimal.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py). The idea is: early multi-root scouting, score-gap pruning at fixed stages, then an ambiguity-triggered late duel between champion and runner-up, plus selective local backward repair only when late previews remain close or uncertain. This targets the current weak high-beta region without wasting low-beta budget.\n\nI inspected the injected baseline table and the compact history/snapshots in the context pack, especially:\n- beta-matched baseline ceilings: `10 / 20 / 36 / 48 / 64` NFE for `beta=0 / .25 / .5 / .75 / 1.0`\n- latest round `r0003`: `0.7852@10`, `0.8264@20`, `0.8358@36`, `0.8396@48`, `0.8400@61.668`\n- prior in-band best `r0002` where relevant: `0.8359@36`, `0.8373@46.752`, `0.8404@61.884`\n- baseline rewards: `0.6765`, `0.8021`, `0.8366`, `0.8440`, `0.8473`\n\nThe exact beta schedule is monotone in willingness to spend compute:\n- `beta=0.0`: single-root preview ladder to `10` NFE.\n- `beta=0.25`: `2` roots, stages at scout/mid/final, no backward repair, target `20`.\n- `beta=0.5`: `3` roots, keep `2` finalists, late duel, target `36`.\n- `beta=0.75`: `4` roots, keep `2` finalists, late duel plus `1` mixed-noise repair child, target `48`.\n- `beta=1.0`: `4` roots, preserve `3` finalists deeper into the run, late duel plus up to `2` mixed-noise repair children, target `64`.\nThis is behaviorally new relative to the recent best controller because it does not just swap late previews for backward children. It adds a distinct mechanism: score-gap/uncertainty-gated duel confirmation, then anchor-ranked repair candidate selection with bounded child count.\n\nTargeted weakness and expected effect:\n- Main target this round is `beta=0.75` and `beta=1.0`.\n- `beta=0.75` was still below the beta-matched ODE baseline at equal NFE, and `beta=1.0` had a stronger prior round than the latest one.\n- The repair is “better allocation inside band,” not raw NFE increase: keep more credible late diversity, confirm only when the top gap is small, and spend backward only on late ambiguous anchors.\n\nTarget-NFE reflection:\n- `beta=0.0`, ceiling/band `10 / [10,10]`: underuse not expected; policy is exactly pinned to 10 with the same successful single-root preview behavior.\n- `beta=0.25`, ceiling/band `20 / [18,20]`: any large underuse would be unjustified, so the policy uses two roots and a final single winner; no backward branch to avoid wasting budget where the controller already beats baseline.\n- `beta=0.5`, ceiling/band `36 / [32,36]`: mild underuse would be bad here because it is still slightly below baseline; the duel keeps two candidates alive to spend near band on useful late evidence.\n- `beta=0.75`, ceiling/band `48 / [44,48]`: prior weakness looked like poor allocation more than missing raw NFE; I adjusted toward late duel plus one repair child so extra spend goes to confirmation/refinement rather than blind full completions.\n- `beta=1.0`, ceiling/band `64 / [60,64]`: first draft risked conservative underuse, so I revised it to preserve three finalists to the last stage and allow up to two repair children; this should use the ceiling more fully without exceeding it.\n\nChecks run:\n- `python -m py_compile flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py`\n- a small toy `FlowTTSEnv` dry run to validate public-API usage and budget gating\n- I did not run the full SD3.5/PickScore eval locally\n\nMain risks:\n- The late ambiguity gates may still be too conservative if PickScore gaps are noisy at `t=1`.\n- `beta=1.0` repair children may still not outperform simply confirming more finalists.\n- `beta=0.5` remains close to baseline, so preserving two finalists could help or could slightly over-diversify.\n\nIf you want, I can also give a compact action-budget accounting for each beta from the new schedule in SD35 step units."}}
